From: David Hamner <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.security.authentication.onlineid: a ticket request is answered

While it looks for a license, Office asks the online identity API for a
service ticket of the Microsoft account system: an
OnlineIdServiceTicketRequest for a service and policy, then
OnlineIdSystemAuthenticator.Default.GetTicketAsync. Every method of the
DLL was E_NOTIMPL, so the licensing's first step failed at the request
instead of at the answer.

The request object (service, policy), the authenticator's application
id and the ticket operation exist now. There is no Microsoft account
service here to issue a ticket, so a request completes at once with
OnlineIdSystemTicketStatus_Error and ERROR_NOT_FOUND and no identity --
how a machine without that service answers. A work account's licensing
does not need such a ticket (it runs on the account's own token, 1479);
this only makes the call behave as the API says.

Gate: test/onlineid-ticket-gate.sh. Mutant:
SG_MUTANT_ONLINEID_NO_TICKET_REQUEST.
---
--- a/dlls/windows.security.authentication.onlineid/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/windows.security.authentication.onlineid/Makefile.in
@@ -5,4 +5,5 @@
 	authenticator.c \
 	classes.idl \
 	main.c \
+	objects.c \
 	ticket.c
